cff-version: 1.2.0
title: karyoratio
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite both the software itself
  and the method it implements (Mittnik et al. 2016).
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Solymosi
    given-names: Norbert
    orcid: 'https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5246-4151'
repository-code: 'https://github.com/solymosin/karyoratio'
abstract: >-
  Chromosome coverage ratios computed directly from an indexed BAM file.
  By default it computes Rx, the X-to-autosome read ratio of Mittnik et al.
  (2016), and estimates genetic sex from it. Unlike existing tools it is
  species-agnostic, requires no Y chromosome, normalises against the full
  autosome set, and reports a confidence interval together with a validity
  criterion. A companion script calibrates the decision thresholds for a new
  species by simulation.
keywords:
  - bioinformatics
  - genomics
  - sex determination
  - non-model organisms
  - low-coverage sequencing
  - conservation genetics
license: MIT
references:
  - type: article
    authors:
      - family-names: Mittnik
        given-names: Alissa
      - family-names: Wang
        given-names: Chuan-Chao
      - family-names: Svoboda
        given-names: Jiří
      - family-names: Krause
        given-names: Johannes
    title: >-
      A molecular approach to the sexing of the triple burial at the Upper
      Paleolithic site of Dolní Věstonice
    journal: PLoS ONE
    year: 2016
    volume: 11
    issue: 10
    start: e0163019
    doi: 10.1371/journal.pone.0163019
